{"parentUuid":"143b7e95-a06d-41d0-aa2f-ff374ac433c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAq6gBQehuorXzcUMRYC4C","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"IPASIR-UP SAT 2023 paper Fazekas Niemetz Preiner Reynolds Barbosa Biere user propagator interface\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - reposiTUm\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/handle/20.500.12708/193053\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - reposiTUm - TU Wien\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/handle/20.500.12708/193053?mode=full\"},{\"title\":\"Supplementary material of submission \\\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\\\"\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/8003683\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Vienna, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/publications/2023/FazekasNPKSB-SAT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Katalin Fazekas - Homepage\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"CEUR-WS.org/Vol-3429 - Satisfiability Modulo Theories 2023\",\"url\":\"https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3429/\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"Awards - SAT 2023\",\"url\":\"https://satisfiability.org/SAT23/pages/awards.html\"}]\n\nI found the paper you're looking for! Here are the key details:\n\n## Paper Information\n\nThe paper \"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\" was authored by Katalin Fazekas, Aina Niemetz, Mathias Preiner, Markus Kirchweger, Stefan Szeider, and Armin Biere, and was presented at the 26th International Conference on Theory and Applications of Satisfiability Testing (SAT 2023).\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nThe paper proposes a general interface to inspect and influence the internal behaviour of CDCL SAT solvers, with the goal of capturing essential functionalities that simplify use cases requiring finer-grained interaction with the SAT solver than provided via the standard IPASIR interface.\n\nThe authors extended CaDiCaL with the IPASIR-UP interface and evaluated it on two representative use cases: enumerating graphs within the SAT modulo Symmetries framework (SMS), and as the main CDCL(T) SAT engine of the SMT solver cvc5.\n\n## Recognition\n\nThe paper \"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\" was recognized with an award at SAT 2023.\n\nThe paper is available through multiple sources, including the official conference proceedings at DROPS (Dagstuhl) and various institutional repositories.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c8109b40-ea36-4a41-8edf-7a45f25fe966","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:36.177Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"143b7e95-a06d-41d0-aa2f-ff374ac433c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8df44b6b-25c9-426b-bfdf-42ed5595c751","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJKfhbfgCvz9hE9THcJXD3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL 2.2 IPASIR-UP external propagator C++ API callbacks documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/src/cadical.hpp at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCal in cadical_sys - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical-sys/latest/cadical_sys/struct.CaDiCal.html\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Vienna, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/publications/2023/FazekasNPKSB-SAT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-SMT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL A CaDiCaL Integration into CDCL(T )\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-CENTAUR23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cadical::Solver - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical/0.1.11/cadical/struct.Solver.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about CaDiCaL 2.2 and its IPASIR-UP external propagator C++ API callbacks documentation:\n\n## Key Documentation Sources\n\nExample implementations of external propagators have been added as a file `test/api/example_propagators.cpp` in CaDiCaL 2.2, which serves as a primary documentation resource for the API.\n\n## Main IPASIR-UP Callbacks\n\nIPASIR-UP provides a callback (with prefix \"cb_\") to interact with the external propagator in each of the five states, and the propagator is being notified about changes to the trail.\n\nThe main callback functions include:\n- **cb_propagate** - for external propagation\n- **cb_add_external** - for adding learned clauses\n- **cb_add_reason** - for providing conflict explanations\n\n## API Connection Functions\n\nUsers can connect an external propagator via the `connect_external_propagator` function, and disconnect via `disconnect_external_propagator`. After connection, every related variable must be marked as 'observed' using the `add_observed_var` function.\n\n## Recent Changes in CaDiCaL 2.2\n\nMany of the requirements of each IPASIR-UP-related solver function have been made explicit, and additional input checks have been added for the arguments of the related callback functions. Example propagators in `test/api/example_propagators.cpp` include code comments demonstrating the newly introduced error messages that can be triggered by misusing the IPASIR-UP interface.\n\nFor the complete C++ API documentation, you can access the header file at the CaDiCaL GitHub repository at `src/cadical.hpp` and the example implementations at `test/api/example_propagators.cpp`.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1d342836-e12c-4f36-8963-147ebe68cc27","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:39.448Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8df44b6b-25c9-426b-bfdf-42ed5595c751","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e2a182d5-b96d-4b6b-ba9f-4d727f804b23","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013HXrrjLNNReimDuGTS8Xg3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cvc5 user propagator CDCL(T) IPASIR-UP CaDiCaL implementation source code\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL(T ): CaDiCaL as CDCL(T ) Engine in cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/talks/Preiner-Shonan23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL A CaDiCaL Integration into CDCL(T )\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-CENTAUR23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Vienna, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/publications/2023/FazekasNPKSB-SAT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Supplementary material of submission \\\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\\\"\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/8003683\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL SAT Conference, July 7, 2023\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/talks/sat2023_talk.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-SMT23.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's comprehensive information about the cvc5 user propagator, CDCL(T), IPASIR-UP, and CaDiCaL implementation:\n\n## Overview\n\nIPASIR-UP extends IPASIR with User Propagators, providing a standardized interface for integrating custom reasoning with CDCL SAT solvers. The CDCL(T) framework requires tight integration with the SAT solver to allow the theory layer to interact with the SAT solver during search in an online fashion.\n\n## CaDiCaL Implementation in cvc5\n\nThe integration of CaDiCaL via IPASIR-UP in cvc5 required approximately 500 lines of C++ code for implementing the interface (approximately 800 including comments). More specifically, the integration via IPASIR-UP consists of approximately 700 C++ lines of code for integration.\n\nThe CaDiCaL integration fully utilizes the IPASIR-UP notification and callback interface, including functions like notify_assignment for constructing partial assignments for observed theory literals, notify new decision level and notify_backtrack for managing incremental solver state, cb_propagate for theory propagations, cb_add_reason_clause_lit for theory explanations, cb_decide for custom decision heuristics, and cb_add_external_clause_lit.\n\n## Source Code Availability\n\nThe most recent versions of the tools are available at: (1) CaDiCaL: https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical (2) cvc5: https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5\n\n## Performance and Advantages\n\nWith CaDiCaL through IPASIR-UP, cvc5 solved an additional 1080 instances and was approximately 2× faster in several logics, with 13 out of 19 divisions improved. Any SAT solver implementing IPASIR-UP can easily replace CaDiCaL, and the integration supports all cvc5 features.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e9b0cd69-6871-4cb2-afb2-7db11368e5d4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:39.752Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2a182d5-b96d-4b6b-ba9f-4d727f804b23","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0db316a6-63c8-4527-a0af-478c0a8836d4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F3EYyAfsioE97qje3P22xc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SMS SAT modulo symmetries IPASIR-UP user propagator graph enumeration\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT Modulo Symmetries for Graph Generation and Enumeration | ACM Transactions on Computational Logic\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3670405\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"},{\"title\":\"SAT modulo Symmetries\",\"url\":\"https://sat-modulo-symmetries.readthedocs.io/en/latest/\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Vienna, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/publications/2023/FazekasNPKSB-SAT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"Satisfiability Modulo User Propagators | Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research\",\"url\":\"https://jair.org/index.php/jair/article/view/16163\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Modulo Symmetries: A Survey Stefan Szeider\",\"url\":\"https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-4116/invited1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Co-Certificate Learning with SAT Modulo Symmetries\",\"url\":\"https://inspirehep.net/literature/2669989\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Modulo Symmetries for Graph Generation and Enumeration\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/382795729_SAT_Modulo_Symmetries_for_Graph_Generation_and_Enumeration\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - reposiTUm\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/handle/20.500.12708/193053\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about these topics. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## SAT Modulo Symmetries (SMS) and IPASIR-UP\n\nSAT Modulo Symmetries (SMS) is a framework and software package for isomorph-free generation and enumeration of graphs under constraints. Constraints for SMS can be specified declaratively, in a combination of propositional logic (DIMACS) and custom extensions, and solved using specially adapted SAT solvers.\n\n### Core Approach\n\nSMS proposes a novel approach for constraint-based graph generation and enumeration that utilizes the interaction between a Conflict-Driven Clause Learning (CDCL) SAT solver and a special propagator excluding lexicographically non-minimal graphs during the search. The symmetry propagator checks partially generated graphs for minimality with respect to a lexicographic ordering during the solving process.\n\n### IPASIR-UP Interface\n\nThe IPASIR-UP paper proposes a general interface to inspect and influence the internal behaviour of CDCL SAT solvers, capturing the essential functionalities that simplify use cases requiring more fine-grained interaction with the SAT solver than provided via the standard IPASIR interface.\n\nSMS uses CaDiCaL with the new IPASIR-UP interface which supports custom propagators, integrating an implementation of MinCheck written in C++ to add symmetry-breaking clauses during search.\n\n### Applications to Graph Enumeration\n\nThe approach is instantiated by generating extremal graphs with certain restrictions in terms of forbidden subgraphs and diameter. To exhaustively generate all isomorph-free objects with a given property, a clause forbidding each object found so far is added.\n\nThe source code is available at https://github.com/markirch/sat-modulo-symmetries with documentation at https://sat-modulo-symmetries.readthedocs.io/\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0067e783-932f-40be-a0a1-bc5a51a379be","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:40.892Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0db316a6-63c8-4527-a0af-478c0a8836d4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
