{"parentUuid":"4c91bdd6-a478-48f0-a56b-a965402980f6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsJynvSJ7R7DtpLT3gG1un","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your interest in IPASIR-UP callback specifications, but I must inform you that the provided content is a compressed PDF binary stream that cannot be reliably parsed as plain text. The raw hex and FlateDecode-compressed data does not yield readable C++ function signatures or semantic contracts in this format.\n\nTo extract the exact callback specifications you need, I recommend:\n\n1. **Access the original PDF directly** via the paper's official publication channel or author repository\n2. **Use a PDF extraction tool** (pdftotext, pypdf, or similar) to convert to plain text first\n3. **Contact the authors** if the specification is unclear from published materials\n\n**What I can tell you from standard IPASIR-UP documentation patterns:**\n\nTypical IPASIR callbacks follow the signature pattern:\n- `void (*notify_*)(void *state, ...)` for notifications\n- Return values are usually `void` or `int` (0 for accept, non-zero for reject)\n- Reason clauses are typically \"zero-terminated literal arrays\" per SAT solver convention\n- Reason completeness contracts specify \"all assigned literals in the implication must appear\"\n\nHowever, **without readable source material**, I cannot provide the exact signatures, invocation timing, or state machine contracts you requested. Please supply the specification in readable text form or provide a direct link to the published paper, and I'll extract the precise details with proper attribution.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 797.2KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778185850767-3b9xel.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"7bfedaec-115f-47cc-9768-d4c4bd0adbae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:56.154Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4c91bdd6-a478-48f0-a56b-a965402980f6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f53d6293-b73c-4416-baec-84261609dc46","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SBnKwdRd98ARpDGq2AivYm","type":"tool_result","content":"I've carefully reviewed the provided web page content, but I must report that **the ExternalPropagator class definition is not included in the visible portion of the cadical.hpp file shown**.\n\nThe page displays lines 1-approximately 1000 of a 1419-line file. The content shows:\n\n- Forward declaration: `class ExternalPropagator;` (around line 474)\n- API functions: `connect_external_propagator()`, `disconnect_external_propagator()`, `add_observed_var()`, `remove_observed_var()`, `reset_observed_vars()`, `is_decision()`, and `force_backtrack()`\n\nHowever, the actual class definition with virtual methods (notify_assignment, notify_new_decision_level, notify_backtrack, cb_check_found_model, cb_decide, cb_propagate, cb_add_reason_clause_lit, cb_has_external_clause, cb_add_external_clause_lit) is **not visible** in this excerpt.\n\nTo obtain the complete ExternalPropagator class definition, new constants/enums, is_lazy flag semantics, and streaming details for reason/external clauses, you would need to:\n\n1. View the full raw file at the GitHub URL\n2. Check related header files (likely tracer.hpp or a dedicated external propagator header)\n3. Consult the CaDiCaL documentation or source repository directly\n\nI cannot provide verbatim code that isn't present in the supplied content."}]},"uuid":"1dc715d1-092e-477d-b19b-64e8ef83a31d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:57.939Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f53d6293-b73c-4416-baec-84261609dc46","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bb5f36a9-9e76-4e44-b25c-20ae7f4af13c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D5ybmjYgkjMmSvobt8bty2","type":"tool_result","content":"# IPASIR-UP Evolution: CaDiCaL 1.x to 2.2\n\n## Major API Changes (Version 2.1.0)\n\nThe transition introduced **breaking changes** to the IPASIR-UP interface:\n\n- **Assignment Notification**: Changed from \"fixed flags passed during notification\" to \"batched into arrays\"\n- **Clause Persistence**: Introduced capability to delete clauses learned from propagators via `is_forgettable` parameter and `are_reasons_forgettable` flag\n- **Backtracking Control**: Added `force_backtrack` function callable during `cb_decide`\n\n## New Capabilities (Version 2.1.0)\n\n- Incremental proof generation (LIDRUP) while using IPASIR-UP\n- Removal of unnecessary backtrack notifications during inprocessing\n- Re-invocation of `cb_propagate` when clauses are added during final model checking\n\n## Enhanced Error Handling (Version 2.2.1)\n\nThe solver now enforces stricter API contracts:\n\n- \"Many requirements of each IPASIR-UP solver function have been made explicit\"\n- Added input validation for callback function arguments\n- Immediate termination on incorrect input (replacing silent recovery attempts)\n- New file `test/api/example_propagators.cpp` demonstrates error messages from misuse\n\n## Additional Improvements (Version 2.2.1)\n\n- `force_backtrack` now permitted during `cb_check_found_model`\n- `new_level` argument type changed from `size_t` to `int`\n- `remove_observed_var` and `reset_observed_vars` callable during solving with explicit error handling\n- Updated explanations and comments throughout IPASIR-UP documentation"}]},"uuid":"56a2a937-c0f9-4e0f-8997-b6c34ca31a81","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:01.208Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb5f36a9-9e76-4e44-b25c-20ae7f4af13c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
