{"parentUuid":"e448fedc-49a3-473c-98be-155e726b1f02","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WM3RHCBke7RKfbDMyiiWwa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KfKxG3tea9cjomUQ6PsR7Y","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arminbiere/cadical/master/src/cadical.hpp","prompt":"Find and quote verbatim the entire ExternalPropagator class definition with all virtual methods. Also quote: connect_external_propagator, disconnect_external_propagator, add_observed_var, remove_observed_var, force_backtrack signatures, plus is_lazy, are_reasons_forgettable, is_forgettable flags. Include any comments above each method that explain semantics."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2535,"cache_read_input_tokens":27164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2535,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqrPefwwrhjkU7vDPWS","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"97edf8ce-c6c2-49c1-a0a0-46e8408d8440","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:06.361Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"97edf8ce-c6c2-49c1-a0a0-46e8408d8440","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KfKxG3tea9cjomUQ6PsR7Y","type":"tool_result","content":"# ExternalPropagator Class Definition\n\nHere is the complete ExternalPropagator class:\n\n```cpp\nclass ExternalPropagator {\n\npublic:\n  bool is_lazy = false; // Lazy propagator only checks complete assignments.\n\n  bool are_reasons_forgettable =\n      false; // Reason external clauses can be deleted.\n\n  virtual ~ExternalPropagator () {}\n\n  virtual void notify_assignment (const std::vector<int> &lits) = 0;\n\n  virtual void notify_new_decision_level () = 0;\n  virtual void notify_backtrack (size_t new_level) = 0;\n\n  virtual bool cb_check_found_model (const std::vector<int> &model) = 0;\n\n  virtual int cb_decide () { return 0; };\n\n  virtual int cb_propagate () { return 0; };\n\n  virtual int cb_add_reason_clause_lit (int propagated_lit) {\n    (void) propagated_lit;\n    return 0;\n  };\n\n  virtual bool cb_has_external_clause (bool &is_forgettable) = 0;\n\n  virtual int cb_add_external_clause_lit () = 0;\n};\n```\n\n## Related Solver Methods\n\n**Connection methods:**\n- `void connect_external_propagator (ExternalPropagator *propagator);`\n- `void disconnect_external_propagator ();`\n\n**Variable observation methods:**\n- `void add_observed_var (int var);`\n- `void remove_observed_var (int var);`\n\n**Backtracking control:**\n- `void force_backtrack (int new_level);`"}]},"uuid":"0cb07d28-3e91-456f-8312-71b2a4dc9e7f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:10.424Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"97edf8ce-c6c2-49c1-a0a0-46e8408d8440","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0cb07d28-3e91-456f-8312-71b2a4dc9e7f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WM3RHCBke7RKfbDMyiiWwa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017DfJDpNxvAEmbns4JDvbJ3","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883","prompt":"This is the JAIR journal extended version of \"Satisfiability Modulo User Propagators\". Extract: (1) the complete IPASIR-UP API table with C and C++ signatures, (2) all 10+ callbacks with their semantic contracts and when they fire, (3) lazy vs eager propagation semantics, (4) reason clause completeness requirements (must contain currently-assigned literals), (5) the state machine showing which callbacks are allowed in which solver state (search/check_model/...), (6) what happens if reason is wrong (unsoundness) vs missing (just slower), (7) cvc5 integration: how many LOC, what each callback maps to in CDCL(T), (8) SMS integration: how MinCheck symmetry breaking is implemented as user propagator, (9) any reported performance numbers vs native SAT."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2535,"cache_read_input_tokens":27164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2535,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqrPefwwrhjkU7vDPWS","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb09b1d1-5bc4-4325-9c62-a6f2b06a1c5b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:12.453Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
