{"parentUuid":"844730c4-2d9a-4c03-ab31-eb4627d3e72d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F5qtbb6Gaj5g1WcE9EDZi2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cadical-sys rust IPASIR-UP propagator pyo3 python binding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - PyO3/pyo3: Rust bindings for the Python interpreter · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - PyO3 user guide\",\"url\":\"https://pyo3.rs/v0.12.3/\"},{\"title\":\"PyO3: Rust Bindings for the Python Interpreter | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=25956502\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started - PyO3 user guide\",\"url\":\"https://pyo3.rs/v0.10.1/\"},{\"title\":\"pyo3 - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/pyo3/latest/pyo3/\"},{\"title\":\"Is it possible to make the python binding optional feature? · PyO3/pyo3 · Discussion #3501\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3/discussions/3501\"},{\"title\":\"Calling Rust from Python with pyo3 | HackerNoon\",\"url\":\"https://hackernoon.com/calling-rust-from-python-with-pyo3\"},{\"title\":\"How I published my 1st Rust-Python binding package | by Senhaji Rhazi hamza | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://hamza-senhajirhazi.medium.com/how-i-published-my-1st-rust-python-binding-package-cb44bc4e2e94\"},{\"title\":\"Calling Rust from Python using PyO3 | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=29368530\"},{\"title\":\"pyo3_bindgen - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/pyo3_bindgen/latest/pyo3_bindgen/\"}]\n\nI've searched for your query, but the results primarily return information about PyO3 (a general Rust-to-Python binding framework) rather than specific information about the combination you're looking for: \"cadical-sys,\" \"IPASIR-UP propagator,\" \"pyo3,\" and \"python binding\" together.\n\nThe search results show that PyO3 can be used to write a native Python module in Rust, or to embed Python in a Rust binary, but they don't contain specific documentation about cadical-sys, IPASIR-UP propagators, or their Python bindings.\n\nTo find more specific information about cadical-sys and IPASIR-UP propagator bindings, you might want to:\n- Check GitHub repositories directly for cadical-sys projects\n- Look for SAT solver or constraint solver documentation, as IPASIR-UP relates to incremental SAT solving interfaces\n- Search specifically on Rust package registries like crates.io\n\nWould you like me to search with different terms, such as searching specifically for \"cadical IPASIR\" or \"SAT solver python binding\"?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2e400b37-282c-4c2e-b64a-fbc8b2bf4ed9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:19.079Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"844730c4-2d9a-4c03-ab31-eb4627d3e72d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"df7ab221-37c4-497d-9d82-4777365535bb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015XoKxdi7Tx9BFx2jELKVW1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"pysat python CaDiCaL IPASIR-UP external propagator binding pydical 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - pysathq/pysat: A toolkit for SAT-based prototyping in Python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT Documentation Release 1.9.dev2\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/pysat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solvers’ API (pysat.solvers) — PySAT 1.9.dev2 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Features\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/features/\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Updates\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/updates/\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Universally Accessible SAT Technology Alexey Ignatiev # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://researchmgt.monash.edu/ws/portalfiles/portal/633352589/633348848-oa.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jix/pydical: Python wrapper for the CaDiCaL SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jix/pydical\"},{\"title\":\"pysat/README.rst at master · pysathq/pysat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat/blob/master/README.rst\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Universally Accessible SAT Technology Alexey Ignatiev # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://alexeyignatiev.github.io/assets/pdf/itk-sat24-preprint.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Available CAV Evaluation Artifact Reusable CAV Evaluation Artifact CaDiCaL 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf\"}]\n\nI've found relevant information about your search query. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## PySAT and IPASIR-UP Support\n\nPySAT now supports arbitrary Boolean formulas with on-the-fly clausification and provides (pre-)processing functionality by exposing an interface to CaDiCaL's (version 1.5.3) preprocessor as well as external user-defined engines following the IPASIR-UP interface.\n\n## External Propagator Binding\n\nAn abstract class for creating external user-defined propagators / reasoning engines can be used with solver CaDiCaL 1.9.5 through the IPASIR-UP interface. Currently, the only SAT solver available in PySAT supporting the interface is CaDiCaL 1.9.5.\n\n## Recent Updates (2026)\n\nRecent fixes include implementation of propagate() for CaDiCaL 1.9.5 and added support for CaDiCaL 1.9.5 with linear engine in example scripts.\n\n## Pydical (Alternative Binding)\n\nI also found Pydical, a Python wrapper for CaDiCaL where CaDiCaL is built and included with Pydical's Python extension and can be installed using pip.\n\nThe search results show that PySAT's support for external propagators through the IPASIR-UP interface with CaDiCaL is well-established and actively maintained.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1824aa76-df55-4b8e-aada-49a725f30992","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:20.279Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"df7ab221-37c4-497d-9d82-4777365535bb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cb09b1d1-5bc4-4325-9c62-a6f2b06a1c5b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017DfJDpNxvAEmbns4JDvbJ3","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your detailed request, but I must clarify what I'm looking at: the content provided appears to be **PDF binary/compressed stream data**, not readable text. The file contains:\n\n- Flate-compressed object streams (objects 81, 105, 118, 98, etc.)\n- Embedded image XObjects with alpha masks\n- Font definitions and form XObjects\n- References to external graphics files (./graphics/CDCL_model.pdf)\n\n**I cannot extract the specific technical content you requested** (IPASIR-UP API tables, callback signatures, state machines, cvc5 integration details, SMS integration examples, or performance benchmarks) from this binary-encoded PDF structure.\n\nTo help you, I would need:\n\n1. **Plain text or readable PDF**: A version where the content streams are decompressed or provided as text\n2. **Direct access to figures/tables**: The CDCL model diagram (referenced in object 100) and API documentation tables\n3. **Source document**: A linked paper or technical report with uncompressed content\n\n**What I can confirm from metadata**: The PDF references a model diagram about CDCL (Conflict-Driven Clause Learning) and appears to be an academic paper, but the actual specification details you're requesting are inaccessible in this format.\n\nWould you be able to provide the paper as plain text, or point me to the specific sections in a readable format?\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 422.8KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778185874561-9x1m6x.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"b59d90a1-1e36-407c-8eb8-f05bf0ac6c30","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:20.624Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cb09b1d1-5bc4-4325-9c62-a6f2b06a1c