{"parentUuid":"74fd8159-c63d-4771-8fa9-3d6abcad11a8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_012f5gXRXS31YTeV715hk5wD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VB1AMJBU2egjjw3sk3Ygiy","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arminbiere/cadical/master/test/api/example_propagators.cpp","prompt":"Quote verbatim the simplest complete external propagator example. I need to see: (1) how notify_assignment is implemented, (2) how cb_propagate returns a literal, (3) how cb_add_reason_clause_lit streams the reason clause one literal at a time (terminated by 0?), (4) how cb_has_external_clause and cb_add_external_clause_lit work for adding new clauses mid-search, (5) how is_lazy is used, (6) any state tracking the propagator does (trail of decision levels). Just give me the cleanest example with all method bodies."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2185,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1931,"cache_read_input_tokens":29699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1931,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqspnHxYm4i1d8TwBw7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"58c5df3c-2f12-46d7-a61d-184d4d7b4b7b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:31.275Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"58c5df3c-2f12-46d7-a61d-184d4d7b4b7b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_012f5gXRXS31YTeV715hk5wD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017Dks5qnEDQu7Wce5QwyySG","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kfazekas.github.io/talks/sat2023_talk.pdf","prompt":"From the SAT 2023 IPASIR-UP talk slides, extract: (1) the table/diagram of all callbacks and when they fire, (2) the lifecycle/state machine showing which callbacks fire in which CDCL state (decide/propagate/conflict/restart/check_model), (3) reason clause semantics: must reason cover the literal at the trail level it was propagated at?, (4) is_lazy semantics, (5) the SMS minimality propagator example, (6) any pseudo-code for a propagator skeleton. Quote slide content directly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2185,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1931,"cache_read_input_tokens":29699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1931,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqspnHxYm4i1d8TwBw7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"53af96d6-3ee4-4a77-a3d1-f65b101a3882","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:35.460Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"58c5df3c-2f12-46d7-a61d-184d4d7b4b7b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VB1AMJBU2egjjw3sk3Ygiy","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the content provided, here's the simplest complete external propagator example with all method bodies shown:\n\n**ActivePropagator** demonstrates the core patterns you're asking about:\n\n1. **notify_assignment**: Updates internal assignment maps for each literal in the batch, maintaining a decision-level trail:\n   ```cpp\n   observed_trail.top().push_back(lit);\n   hole_map[hole_id].assign(pig_id, lit);\n   pigeon_map[pig_id].assign(hole_id, lit);\n   ```\n\n2. **cb_propagate returns a literal** after checking propagation conditions:\n   ```cpp\n   if (hole_map[h].propagates()) {\n     int lit = -1 * ph(hole_map[h].next_unassigned_pos, h);\n     reason_map[lit] = -1 * ph(hole_map[h].get_val(), h);\n     return lit;\n   }\n   return 0; // no propagation\n   ```\n\n3. **cb_add_reason_clause_lit streams one literal per call**, terminated by 0:\n   ```cpp\n   if (clause.empty()) explain_propagation(propagated_lit);\n   int lit = clause[next_lit++];\n   if (!lit) clause.clear();\n   return lit;\n   ```\n\n4. **cb_has_external_clause and cb_add_external_clause_lit** build conflict clauses mid-search, using similar streaming mechanics.\n\n5. **is_lazy = false** enables active notification of all assignments and decision levels.\n\n6. **State tracking**: The `observed_trail` stack maintains decision-level nesting; `hole_map` and `pigeon_map` track variable assignments per hole/pigeon."}]},"uuid":"99a9203c-5471-4936-9387-ebe36f4d05dc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:36.014Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"58c5df3c-2f12-46d7-a61d-184d4d7b4b7b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"m