{"parentUuid":"f5aa6824-7827-4d4c-952e-2e9444d83bad","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Request failed with status code 404","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nr297ELCQ6gPCCo3H7bZaX"}]},"uuid":"7279f607-ff68-46d2-8ffd-f38286a1c020","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:39.343Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Request failed with status code 404","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5aa6824-7827-4d4c-952e-2e9444d83bad","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"53af96d6-3ee4-4a77-a3d1-f65b101a3882","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Dks5qnEDQu7Wce5QwyySG","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your detailed request, but I need to be straightforward: the content you've provided appears to be a PDF file encoded in binary/compressed format (PDF stream objects with FlateDecode compression). I cannot reliably extract and read the actual slide content from this raw PDF data.\n\nTo help you effectively, I would need either:\n\n1. **Plain text or markdown** extracted from the slides\n2. **Screenshots or images** of the specific slides\n3. **A link** to the actual SAT 2023 IPASIR-UP presentation materials\n4. **Key slide numbers** so I can focus on specific sections\n\nFrom what you're asking for—callback tables, lifecycle diagrams, reason clause semantics, is_lazy semantics, minimality propagator examples, and propagator skeleton pseudo-code—these are all highly technical topics that deserve accurate representation. Attempting to extract them from compressed PDF streams would likely introduce errors.\n\n**Could you provide the source material in a more accessible format?** Once you do, I'll be happy to:\n- Extract the specific information you need\n- Provide direct quotes (respecting the 125-character limit)\n- Explain the technical concepts clearly\n- Distinguish between exact quotes and my summaries\n\nThis will ensure accuracy for technical content that matters for your work.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 914.5KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778185897686-wf4j5s.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"4cb94302-2dd3-4c09-8150-8b5f57a511cd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:43.648Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"53af96d6-3ee4-4a77-a3d1-f65b101a3882","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"48475428-be49-4617-bf50-14ebfc509cd6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xvy9X2HbG7jn439VVicCZH","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"cb_propagate\" \"cb_add_reason_clause_lit\" implementation example trail backtrack\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"Trail Saving on Backtrack - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7326469/\"},{\"title\":\"2.9. CONFLICT DRIVEN CLAUSE LEARNING (CDCL) 61 Backtrack:\",\"url\":\"https://www.mpi-inf.mpg.de/fileadmin/inf/rg1/script5ws1617.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 03\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/sat/ss23/03/\"},{\"title\":\"2.10. IMPLEMENTING CDCL 71 Resolve:\",\"url\":\"https://www.mpi-inf.mpg.de/fileadmin/inf/rg1/script6ws1617.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Trail Saving on Backtrack | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-51825-7_4\"},{\"title\":\"Refactoring Varisat: 3. Conflict Driven Clause Learning - jix.one\",\"url\":\"https://jix.one/refactoring-varisat-3-cdcl/\"},{\"title\":\"The Implementation - CDCL From Scratch in Python\",\"url\":\"https://kienyew.github.io/CDCL-SAT-Solver-from-Scratch/The-Implementation.html\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict-driven clause learning (CDCL) SAT solvers — CS-E3220: Propositional satisfiability and SAT solvers documentation\",\"url\":\"https://users.aalto.fi/~tjunttil/2020-DP-AUT/notes-sat/cdcl.html\"},{\"title\":\"The DPLL backtracking search procedure — CS-E3220: Propositional satisfiability and SAT solvers documentation\",\"url\":\"https://users.aalto.fi/~tjunttil/2021-DP-AUT/notes-sat/dpll.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about these SAT solver callback functions in the IPASIR-UP interface. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## cb_propagate and cb_add_reason_clause_lit\n\nDuring unit propagation, the user can provide additional literals to be propagated through the cb_propagate callback. This callback returns only a literal to be propagated. The propagating clause is not required at this point.\n\nIf during conflict analysis a previous user propagation turns out to be relevant (i.e., necessary to derive the learnt clause), the solver asks for the corresponding reason clause via cb_add_reason_clause_lit, one literal at a time. This is part of what's called a \"delayed lazy explanation\" approach.\n\n## Implementation Context with Trail and Backtracking\n\nFor enumeration with the new interface, the current trail is preserved and backtracked. The callbacks work within the CDCL (Conflict-Driven Clause Learning) framework where backtracking occurs after every conflict, where all literals from one or more decision levels become unassigned before the solver resumes making decisions and performing unit propagations.\n\nThe search results indicate these functions are part of the IPASIR-UP (Incremental Partial Assignment SAT Solver Interface with Uncertainty and propagation callbacks) interface, which extends standard SAT solver functionality to allow external propagators to interact with the solver during the search process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d5178a71-19cb-441f-ab10-15f4c0128538","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:45.390Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"48475428-be49-4617-bf50-14ebfc509cd6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
