{"parentUuid":"dba837f0-628e-4f71-bb5e-a607ef48c6f3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015BpBTJxA5st1tMSipKtBNf","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pydical and External Propagators\n\nBased on the provided documentation, I cannot find any evidence that pydical exposes IPASIR-UP, external propagators, or a `connect_external_propagator` method.\n\n## Project Status\n\nThe author states: \"I've written it for my own use and am sharing it in case someone else has similar requirements. Currently I have no intention to commit on maintaining this long term.\"\n\nAdditionally, they note: \"In the near future I plan to extend CaDiCaL's API to expose some more internals. From that point on Pydical will use my own fork of CaDiCaL, as CaDiCaL does not accept external contributions.\"\n\n## CaDiCaL Version\n\nThe documentation does not specify which CaDiCaL version is included, only that \"CaDiCaL is built and included with Pydical's Python extension.\"\n\n## API Coverage\n\nThe wrapper aims to provide \"coverage for the whole C++ API of CaDiCaL\" and \"closely mirrors the solver's C++ API,\" but the README provides no evidence of external propagator support. No abstract Python propagator class is mentioned in the available content."}]},"uuid":"f9cfc2f2-6f95-44c5-aebd-964b8947ba9a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:56.609Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dba837f0-628e-4f71-bb5e-a607ef48c6f3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"29852e38-35e6-468f-97b2-ad6d3041de69","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XD2jNb6nMHLLA8ZSkDwP24","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PySAT propagator CaDiCaL \"connect_propagator\" example code python\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"PySAT Documentation Release 1.9.dev2\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/pysat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solvers’ API (pysat.solvers) — PySAT 1.9.dev2 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pysathq/pysat: A toolkit for SAT-based prototyping in Python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Features\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/features/\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Updates\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/updates/\"},{\"title\":\"pysat/pysat/solvers.py at master · pysathq/pysat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat/blob/master/pysat/solvers.py\"},{\"title\":\"circuitgraph.sat API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://circuitgraph.github.io/circuitgraph/sat.html\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Universally Accessible SAT Technology Alexey Ignatiev # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://research.monash.edu/files/633352589/633348848-oa.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Homework 2: SAT & SMT solvers — CS 395T: Systems Verification and Synthesis\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.utexas.edu/~bornholt/courses/cs395t-22sp/homework/hw2/\"},{\"title\":\"pysathq/pysat | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/pysathq/pysat\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about using `connect_propagator` with PySAT, CaDiCaL, and external propagators:\n\n## Overview\n\nOnce an engine is implemented, it should be attached to a solver object by calling `connect_propagator()` of CaDiCaL. Currently, the only SAT solver available in PySAT supporting the interface is CaDiCaL 1.9.5.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe propagator will then need to inform the solver what variable it requires to observe. The implementation of this functionality builds on the use of the IPASIR-UP interface.\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\nThe only expected argument is propagator, which must be an object of a class inheriting from the abstract class Propagator. An abstract class for creating external user-defined propagators / reasoning engines to be used with solver Cadical through the IPASIR-UP interface. All user-defined propagators should inherit the interface of this abstract class, i.e. all the below methods need to be properly defined.\n\n## Example Reference\n\nA user is encouraged to examine the source code of BooleanEngine in order to see how an external reasoning engine can be implemented and attached to CaDiCaL 1.9.5. A simple example Boolean constraint propagator inheriting from the class Propagator. The idea is to exemplify the use of external reasoning engines.\n\nThe search results reference the official PySAT documentation and GitHub repository, but don't include the complete example code itself. For detailed example code, you would need to consult the PySAT documentation directly or examine the source code of the BooleanEngine implementation referenced in the docs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e368b4b9-5ae4-481b-b5bc-dc34306780c0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:31:59.441Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"29852e38-35e6-468f-97b2-ad6d3041de69","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
