{"parentUuid":"c5363410-7b73-40be-a3ef-f11b7f6a2ff0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013NE7Q7cSJw6zfytD8mNpw9","type":"tool_result","content":"# Propagator Abstract Class\n\n```python\nclass Propagator(object):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.is_lazy = False\n\n    def on_assignment(self, lit: int, fixed: bool = False) -> None:\n        pass\n\n    def on_new_level(self) -> None:\n        pass\n\n    def on_backtrack(self, to: int) -> None:\n        pass\n\n    def check_model(self, model: List[int]) -> bool:\n        pass\n\n    def decide(self) -> int:\n        return 0\n\n    def propagate(self) -> List[int]:\n        return []\n\n    def provide_reason(self, lit: int) -> List[int]:\n        pass\n\n    def add_clause(self) -> List[int]:\n        return []\n```\n\n# Solver Registration Pattern\n\n```python\nsolver = Solver(name='cadical195', bootstrap_with=some_formula)\n\nengine = BooleanEngine(...)\nsolver.connect_propagator(engine)\n\nfor var in range(some_variables):\n    solver.observe(var)\n```\n\n# BooleanEngine Key Methods\n\nThe example engine implements constraint propagation through: initialization accepting constraint lists, state tracking via `on_assignment()` and backtracking callbacks, literal propagation via the `propagate()` method returning inferred literals, and conflict explanation through `provide_reason()` and `add_clause()` for generating learned clauses when assignments violate constraints."}]},"uuid":"8075f567-d7e9-4c94-aed7-a6a5f2114169","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:15.697Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c5363410-7b73-40be-a3ef-f11b7f6a2ff0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
