{"parentUuid":"1a98bfb2-b3c8-4739-a619-f72b1f32baab","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C9apgawTthV4M2PaecbGPG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"IPASIR-UP\" reason clause soundness incorrect \"false positive\" wrong learned clause\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"IPASIR - Ipasir\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.utexas.edu/~moore/acl2/manuals/current/manual/index-seo.php/IPASIR____IPASIR\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-SMT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL(T ): CaDiCaL as CDCL(T ) Engine in cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/talks/Preiner-Shonan23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[IPASIR UP] Search with uninitialized search limits · Issue #106 · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/issues/106\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/src/cadical.hpp at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL SAT Conference, July 7, 2023\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/talks/sat2023_talk.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Reasoning-2\",\"url\":\"https://cis.temple.edu/~wangp/3203-AI/Lecture/Reasoning-2.htm\"},{\"title\":\"soundness vs completeness\",\"url\":\"https://mudongliang.github.io/2017/04/09/soundness-vs-completeness.html\"}]\n\nI found search results related to IPASIR-UP (User Propagators for CDCL SAT solvers), but the results do not contain specific information about reason clause soundness issues, false positives, or incorrectness in learned clauses related to IPASIR-UP.\n\nThe search results show that IPASIR-UP is a general interface to inspect and influence the internal behavior of CDCL SAT solvers, with the goal to capture essential functionalities for fine-grained interaction with the SAT solver. The interface allows users to add propagations (without adding reason clauses), dictate decisions and phases, and add new clauses anytime.\n\nHowever, the search results do not specifically address any soundness issues with reason clauses, false positives in learned clauses, or any documented bugs or problems with incorrect learned clauses in IPASIR-UP. If you're looking for information about a specific known issue or vulnerability related to reason clause soundness in IPASIR-UP, you may want to check:\n\n1. The official issue tracker for CaDiCaL (the SAT solver implementing IPASIR-UP)\n2. Academic papers discussing IPASIR-UP implementation details\n3. Community forums or mailing lists for SAT solver development\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about IPASIR-UP or related SAT solver issues?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b3f801ce-f7ac-4b49-9709-2101e44c26d6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:26.020Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1a98bfb2-b3c8-4739-a619-f72b1f32baab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7536736c-f761-4375-957a-72853d1ebe2d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8dfd7d49-883e-40c9-8948-d7864c6a5fee","agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013rm5YMM3VhFQTeWhZQH4X9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"IPASIR-UP\" 2025 routing pathfinding grid CSP user propagator practical experience\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/talks/Niemetz-SMT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/sat/FazekasNPKSB23.html\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Vienna, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~niemetz/publications/2023/FazekasNPKSB-SAT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - reposiTUm\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/handle/20.500.12708/193053\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL SAT Conference, July 7, 2023\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/talks/sat2023_talk.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 Armin Biere1,2(B) , Tobias Faller1 , Katalin Fazekas3\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24-Springer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PathPlanning · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PathPlanning\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about IPASIR-UP, though the results don't specifically cover routing, pathfinding, and grid CSP with practical experience from 2025. Here's what the search reveals:\n\n## IPASIR-UP Overview\n\nIPASIR-UP is an interface for User Propagators for CDCL, a SAT solver extension. Modern SAT solvers are frequently embedded as sub-reasoning engines into more complex tools for addressing problems beyond Boolean satisfiability, including solvers for Satisfiability Modulo Theories (SMT), combinatorial optimization, model enumeration and counting.\n\n## Key Functionality\n\nIPASIR-UP proposes a general interface to inspect and influence the internal behavior of CDCL SAT solvers, capturing essential functionalities sufficient to simplify and improve use cases requiring fine-grained interaction with the SAT solver beyond the standard IPASIR interface.\n\nWhile an external propagator is connected, users can notify the solver that a variable is \"relevant\" by declaring it as an observed variable via add_observed_var, and when not in Solving state, observed variables can be removed via remove_observed_var, with all IPASIR-UP calls involving observed variables only.\n\n## Use Cases\n\nIPASIR-UP was evaluated on two representative use cases: enumerating graphs with certain properties via SAT Modulo Symmetries, and integrating CaDiCaL as the main CDCL(T) SAT engine in the SMT solver cvc5.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about practical experience with routing, pathfinding, grid-based CSP problems, or any 2025 developments. For more specific details on those applications, you may need to search for academic papers or technical blogs specifically addressing grid-based routing with IPASIR-UP.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e25b083e-0816-4c1c-a691-509ad4cb2528","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:32:29.064Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7536736c-f761-4375-957a-72853d1ebe2d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e25b083e-0816-4c1c-a691-509ad4cb2528","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89b891b3e3123556","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QdFXSvdBnmBQYnJaNPQ3dT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me write the report.\n\n---\n\n# IPASIR-UP 深入调研报告（PoC 可执行版）\n\n## 1. 论文与 callback 完整列表\n\n**论文：** Fazekas, Niemetz, Preiner, Kirchweger, Szeider, Biere, \"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL\", SAT 2023（获奖论文），JAIR 81 (2024) 扩展版。PDF 是压缩流，WebFetch 无法直接抽文本，但 NEWS.md + 头文件 + PySAT 文档已足够。\n\n**CaDiCaL `ExternalPropagator` 抽象类（src/cadical.hpp 直读，verbatim）：**\n\n```cpp\nclass ExternalPropagator {\npublic:\n  bool is_lazy = false;                    // 仅在完整模型时检查\n  bool are_reasons_forgettable = false;    // 解释子句可被删除\n\n  virtual void notify_assignment (const std::vector<int> &lits) = 0;\n  virtual void notify_new_decision_level () = 0;\n  virtual void notify_backtrack (size_t new_level) = 0;\n  virtual bool cb_check_found_model (const std::vector<int> &model) = 0;\n  virtual int  cb_decide () { return 0; }                     // 返回字面量或 0\n  virtual int  cb_propagate () { return 0; }                  // 返回要传播的字面量或 0\n  virtual int  cb_add_reason_clause_lit (int propagated_lit); // 流式吐字面量，0 = 结束\n  virtual bool cb_has_external_clause (bool &is_forgettable) = 0;\n  virtual int  cb_add_external_clause_lit () = 0;             // 流式吐字面量，0 = 结束\n};\n```\n\n**Solver 侧（同文件）：** `connect_external_propagator(ExternalPropagator*)`、`disconnect_external_propagator()`、`add_observed_var(int)`、`remove_observed_var(int)`、`force_backtrack(int new_level)`（2.1+ 允许在 `cb_decide` 和 `cb_check_found_model` 中调用）。\n\n**契约要点：**\n- `notify_assignment` 在 2.1 后改为**批量数组**（不是单个字面量）。\n- `cb_propagate` 只返回 1 个字面量；CaDiCaL 在冲突分析中**真正用到**这个传播时才会回调 `cb_add_reason_clause_lit` 流式问 reason —— 这就是 \"delayed lazy explanation\"，省掉一大堆 reason 构造开销。\n- Reason 子句必须是 propagated_lit 的合法蕴含（`assigned_falsified ⇒ propagated_lit` 在原 CNF 下可证），**否则破坏 soundness**，求解器会 UNSAT 一个本来 SAT 的实例（这是真错误，不是慢）。\n- `is_lazy=true` 时只在每个 SAT 候选模型上调一次 `cb_check_found_model`，搜索期不传播。\n- `cb_has_external_clause` 在每个决策点都会被问，把外加子句写成 `is_forgettable=true` 的话求解器可以丢，写 `false` 求解器必须留 —— **这就是跨次保留 learned clauses 的正确旋钮**。\n\n来源：[cadical.hpp 主线](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp)、[NEWS.md](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md)、[example_propagators.cpp](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/test/api/example_propagators.cpp)。\n\n## 2. CaDiCaL 2.2 实装状态\n\nNEWS.md 直读：\n- **2.1.0 是分水岭**：`notify_assignment` 改批量数组、新增 `is_forgettable`/`are_reasons_forgettable`、`force_backtrack` 加入 `cb_decide`、IPASIR-UP 期间支持 LIDRUP 增量证明、模型检查中加子句会重新触发 `cb_propagate`。\n- **2.2.1**：所有 callback 加严格输入校验（误用立即报错而不是静默走错），`force_backtrack` 允许在 `cb_check_found_model` 中调，`new_level` 类型从 `size_t` 改 `int`。\n- 例子在 `test/api/example_propagators.cpp`（鸽笼问题 `ActivePropagator`）—— 这是官方权威 reference。\n\n**结论：所有 callback 已实装、稳定，2.2 是干净的 PoC 起点。**\n\n## 3. 现有 IPASIR-UP 用例\n\n- **cvc5 / CaDiCaL(T)**：约 700 行 C++ 把 SMT 理论层接进来，全套 callback 都用上（`notify_assignment` 构建 partial assignment、`cb_propagate` 做理论传播、`cb_add_reason_clause_lit` 做理论解释、`cb_decide` 自定义决策、`cb_add_external_clause_lit` 加 lemma）。**比旧路径多解 1080 个 SMT-LIB 实例，部分逻辑约 2× 提速**（19 个 division 改善 13 个）。\n- **SMS（Kirchweger/Szeider）**：图枚举的 MinCheck（lex-min 同构破坏）作为 user propagator 接 CaDiCaL，是把\"非纯 CNF 性质\"塞进 CDCL 最经典的工程模板，源码在 [sat-modulo-symmetries](https://github.com/markirch/sat-modulo-symmetries)，文档 [readthedocs](https://sat-modulo-symmetries.readthedocs.io/en/latest/)。\n- **routing/pathfinding** 没找到公开案例，需要原创设计。\n\n## 4. Python 绑定现状\n\n| 选项 | IPASIR-UP 暴露 | 可用性 |\n|------|---|---|\n| **PySAT** ([engines.py](https://github.com/pysathq/pysat/blob/master/pysat/engines.py)) | **是** —— 抽象类 `Propagator`：`on_assignment(lit, fixed)`、`on_new_level()`、`on_backtrack(to)`、`check_model(model)`、`decide()`、`propagate()` 返回字面量 list、`provide_reason(lit)` 返 list、`add_clause()` 返 list。Solver 端用 `Solver(name='cadical195').connect_propagator(engine)` + `solver.observe(var)` | **当前最稳路径**。但锁死 CaDiCaL **1.9.5**（不是 2.2），用不到 `is_forgettable` / `are_reasons_forgettable` / `force_backtrack` 等 2.x 红利 |\n| **pydical** | **不暴露** propagator，作者明确要 fork CaDiCaL 才扩 API，不维护 | 不要用 |\n| **cadical-sys + PyO3** | sys crate 是 raw FFI，需要自己写 trait + PyO3 wrapper | 工程量 ~ 2-3 周（要写 unsafe FFI 包装、Send/Sync 安全、回调跨语言边界），收益是拿到 CaDiCaL 2.2 |\n| **自己写 pybind11 wrapper** | 直接绑 `ExternalPropagator` 虚类 | ~ 1 周，~300 行 C++，最干净但要会 pybind11 跨语言虚函数派发（`PYBIND11_OVERRIDE_PURE`） |\n\n**推荐：PoC 阶段用 PySAT（CaDiCaL 1.9.5），跑通后如果性能/2.2 特性是瓶颈，再花 1 周写 pybind11 wrapper 升 2.2。**\n\n## 5. routing_subproblem 替换可行性\n\n读了 `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\routing_subproblem.py`（1018 行）和 `binding_subproblem.py`（599 行）：\n\n- **routing 是状态机模型**：每格×每层×(flow_in 方向集, flow_out 方向集) 一个 `r_var` 布尔（`NewBoolVar`），通过 `AddImplication` 串成路径合法性约束 + 每个 source/sink 端口的入/出守恒。**几乎全部布尔 + 蕴含**，没有 CP-SAT 的 interval/cumulative/circuit 高级约束 —— **完美适合迁到 SAT**。\n- **难点**：commodity-scoped 多商品流的容量约束（多商品共享同一格的 0/1 占用），需要在 propagator 里维护\"每 commodity 的部分路径前沿\"做增量 reachability 检查。\n- **user propagator 的甜点**：每次 outer search 候选都跑同一个布局核心 + 不同端口集，**learned clauses（\"这一组端口在这片占用下不可路由\"）跨次复用** —— 这正是 OR-Tools 抛弃的东西，也是 D' 方案的核心收益。\n\n**工程量：** 把 routing 转成纯 CNF + 做一个 `RoutingPropagator(Propagator)`：\n- CNF 编码：每格状态独热 + 邻接守恒 + 端口源汇守恒 ≈ 2-3 周（替换现有 ~500 行 CP-SAT 建模）\n- Propagator 维护\"已激活格 + 连通分量\"，`propagate()` 检测断头/孤岛 → 返回禁用某 cell-state 字面量；`provide_reason()` 返回\"这些已激活格的并集 ⇒ 当前格不能这么连\" ≈ 1.5-2 周\n- 跨次 learned clauses 持久化：把 `cb_has_external_clause` 在 SAT 后导出 nogood 集，下次 `bootstrap_with` 注入 ≈ 2-3 天\n\n**binding 不建议先动**：它包含整数容量算术（每条 line 的吞吐计算），转 SAT 要加 bit-blast 编码，得不偿失。**routing 是正确的 PoC 起点。**\n\n## 6. 学习曲线 / pitfalls\n\n- **soundness 杀手**：reason clause 没有真正蕴含 propagated_lit → 求解器学错的 nogood → 整体 UNSAT 错误。**必须写一个独立的 reason validator**（在 propagate 当时的 partial assignment 上验证 `reason ∧ ¬propagated_lit` 在原 CNF 下不可满足），调试模式跑。\n- **trail 同步坑**：`notify_assignment` 是批量来的，必须按顺序 push 到自己的 trail 栈；`notify_backtrack(to)` 要 pop 到 `to` 这个 level（注意 inprocessing 时 2.1 后会跳过部分回调，要看 NEWS）。\n- **观察变量遗漏**：忘了 `add_observed_var` 的变量不会触发任何 notify，propagator 看到的状态是错的，纯静默 bug。\n- **lazy 模式陷阱**：`is_lazy=true` 只在完整模型上检查，不能用于路径连通这种需要剪枝的约束（会让搜索空间炸）。\n- **PySAT `provide_reason` 必须返回**包含 `lit` 自己的子句（即 `lit ∨ ¬assigned_premises`），漏 `lit` 求解器立即崩。\n\n## 7. 学术 best practices\n\n- **delayed lazy explanation**：`cb_propagate` 不要预算 reason，等 `cb_add_reason_clause_lit` 真问的时候再算 —— SAT23 论文核心优化。\n- **observed var 最小化**：只 observe 真正影响传播的变量，cvc5 经验是过度 observe 让 `notify_assignment` 开销超过收益。\n- **forgettable reasons**：`are_reasons_forgettable=true` 让 CaDiCaL 自己 GC，避免 propagator 持久持有大堆解释子句吃内存。\n- **assumption 配合**：每次 outer 候选用 `solver.solve(assumptions=[port_lits])` 锁定端口，propagator 状态可保留，learned clauses 自动跨次。\n\n## PoC 计划（具体可跑）\n\n**Week 1**（环境 + skeleton）：\n1. `pip install python-sat[aiger,approxmc,cryptosat,pblib]`，确认 `Solver(name='cadical195')` + `connect_propagator` 可用\n2. 复现 PySAT 文档里的 `BooleanEngine` 例子，跑通鸽笼问题 PoC（验证 callback 链路）\n3. 选 1 个最小 routing 实例（5×5 grid、2 端口对），手写 CNF + 一个 trivial `RoutingPropagator`（只在 `check_model` 里验证连通性）\n\n**Week 2-3**（最小可用 propagator）：\n1. 把 routing CNF 编码器从 CP-SAT 翻成纯 SAT（5×5 → 10×10 → 70×70 渐进）\n2. 实现 `propagate()`：增量 reachability（已激活格的并查集），发现某 cell 已被孤立时返回该 cell 的禁用字面量\n3. 实现 `provide_reason(lit)`：返回\"使该 cell 必须激活的端口字面量集\"\n4. 跑独立 reason validator（debug 模式，每次 propagate 都验证 reason 蕴含正确）\n\n**Week 4**（跨次复用 + 集成）：\n1. SAT 后从求解器导出非 forgettable 子句 → JSON 落盘到 `data/checkpoints/learned_clauses_routing.jsonl`\n2. 下次 bootstrap_with 时注入\n3. 对比 baseline：相同 50 个 outer 候选，CP-SAT 路径 vs 新路径的累计求解时间\n\n**数据格式：**\n```json\n{\"campaign_hash\": \"...\", \"subproblem\": \"routing\",\n \"var_map\": {\"cell_3_5_layer0_in_N_out_S\": 1234, ...},  // 字面量 → 语义\n \"learned_clauses\": [[-1234, 56, -789], ...],\n \"source_assumptions\": [...]}\n```\n\n**第一周可交付：**\n- `experiments/ipasir_up/poc/skeleton.py`：PySAT + CaDiCaL 1.9.5 跑通鸽笼，confirm callback 链路\n- 5×5 routing CNF 编码器 + trivial check_model propagator，输出\"建模 N 变量 M 子句、求解 X ms\"\n- 一个 50 行的 `reason_validator.py`，独立验证任何 propagator 的 reason 子句正确性\n\n**总工程量评估（替换 routing 子问题）：** 4-6 周到能跑、3 个月到产品质量并量化收益。比 D' 方案预期收益（跨次复用 learned clauses，预计 routing 阶段 30-50% 加速）合理。\n\n**关键限制：**\n- PySAT 锁 CaDiCaL 1.9.5，缺 2.2 的严格校验和 `is_forgettable`，bug 排查更痛 —— 如果第 2 周 reason soundness 老出错，建议直接跳到 pybind11 wrap 2.2（额外 1 周成本）\n- routing 问题里有部分整数算术（容量匹配），如果 CNF 编码后变量数爆炸（>100k），考虑混合：把整数部分留 CP-SAT（小型 binding 子问题），只 SAT-化纯路径连通性\n\n## 关键链接\n\n- 论文：[IPASIR-UP SAT 2023 (DROPS)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8)、[JAIR 81 (2024) 扩展版](https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/view/16163)\n- CaDiCaL 头文件：[src/cadical.hpp](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp)\n- 官方例子：[test/api/example_propagators.cpp](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/test/api/example_propagators.cpp)\n- API 演进：[cadical NEWS.md](https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md)\n- cvc5 集成 talk：[Preiner Shonan 2023](https://cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/talks/Preiner-Shonan23.pdf)\n- SMS 项目：[sat-modulo-symmetries GitHub](https://github.com/markirch/sat-modulo-symmetries)、[文档](https://sat-modulo-symmetries.readthedocs.io/en/latest/)\n- PySAT propagator：[pysat/engines.py](https://github.com/pysathq/pysat/blob/master/pysat/engines.py)、[PySAT updates](https://pysathq.github.io/updates/)\n- pydical（不推荐）：[github.com/jix/pydical](https://github.com/jix/pydical)\n\n## 涉及到的本地文件\n\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\routing_subproblem.py`（1018 行，PoC 替换目标）\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\binding_subproblem.py`（599 行，**不建议**首批替换）"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":47154,"output_tokens":6029,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens